  Both bugs are fixed[0m[2m. Here's what[0m[2m changed and[0m[2m why:
     
     **`[0m[2minventory.py`**[0m[2m — Added `async[0m[2mio.Lock` and[0m[2m two new methods ([0m[2mpublic[0m[2m interfaces[0m[2m unchanged[0m[2m):
     - `reserve[0m[2m(quantity[0m[2m)`[0m[2m — atom[0m[2mically checks stock and[0m[2m decrements under[0m[2m a[0m[2m lock, eliminating[0m[2m the TOCTOU[0m[2m race between check[0m[2m and decrement that[0m[2m caused overs[0m[2melling[0m[2m
     - `release[0m[2m(quantity)` — returns[0m[2m reserved[0m[2m stock under the[0m[2m same lock, used[0m[2m when payment fails[0m[2m
     
     **`checkout.py[0m[2m`** — Re[0m[2mplaced the three[0m[2m-step check[0m[2m→[0m[2mcharge→decrement[0m[2m flow[0m[2m with reserve[0m[2m→charge→([0m[2mrollback[0m[2m if[0m[2m needed):
     - Reserve[0m[2m stock *[0m[2mfirst* (atom[0m[2mically), then[0m[2m attempt[0m[2m the[0m[2m charge. If the[0m[2m charge fails, release[0m[2m the stock back[0m[2m. This guarantees[0m[2m every successful charge corresponds[0m[2m to exactly one reserved[0m[2m-and[0m[2m-delivered item,[0m[2m eliminating ghost[0m[2m charges.
     - The[0m[2m old `check[0m[2m_stock()` →[0m[2m `decrement()`[0m[2m pattern had[0m[2m a TOCTOU[0m[2m race[0m[2m: multiple coroutines[0m[2m could observe[0m[2m `[0m[2mstock[0m[2m >= quantity[0m[2m`,[0m[2m all[0m[2m proceed to charge,[0m[2m and then all succeed[0m[2m at[0m[2m decrement[0m[2ming[0m[2m —[0m[2m driving stock negative.[0m[2m The atomic[0m[2m `[0m[2mreserve()` prevents[0m[2m this because[0m[2m the lock serial[0m[2mizes the check-and[0m[2m-decrement.
     
     The[0m[2m three invariants hold[0m[2m across[0m[2m all test[0m[2m runs:
